+## Phone-friendly diagnostics
+
+The compliance evidence the pipeline produces is rich, but its
+default UX is a desktop log drill-down: open the Actions tab, click
+the run, click a job, expand the failed step, scroll for the
+`##[error]` line. A reviewer working from a phone can see the red ✗
+and almost nothing else actionable.
+
+Three add-on patterns close that gap. They compose; each can be
+adopted independently.
+
+### Sticky PR-summary comment
+
+A `pr-summary` job runs after the rest of the pipeline, downloads
+every artifact, parses the structured ones (Surefire `.txt`
+summaries, JaCoCo `jacoco.xml`, frontend coverage JSON,
+`trivy-results.json`, `npm-audit.json`, `gitleaks-report.json`,
+`evidence-manifest.json`, Playwright `test-results/`), and
+**upserts a single sticky comment** on the PR via
+`marocchino/sticky-pull-request-comment` with `header: pr-summary`.
+
+Comment shape (top-line first, table next, links last) keeps it
+readable on a phone:
+
+```markdown
+**Status:** ✅ all signals green · `abc1234`
+
+| Signal | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| Backend tests (Surefire) | ✅ 80 run, 0 failed |
+| JaCoCo line / branch | 11.2% / 1.8% |
+| E2E (Playwright) | ✅ 0 failed spec(s) |
+| Trivy findings | ✅ 0 (none) |
+| npm audit (production) | ✅ 0 |
+| Gitleaks | ✅ 0 finding(s) |
+| Evidence manifest | ✅ 10 artifact(s); 0 missing |
+```
+
+Job sketch:
+
+```yaml
+pr-summary:
+  if: always() && github.event_name == 'pull_request'
+  needs: [secrets-scan, test, e2e, vulnerability-scan, sbom, oscal,
+          verify-evidence]
+  permissions:
+    contents: read
+    pull-requests: write
+  steps:
+    - uses: actions/checkout@<sha>
+    - uses: actions/setup-node@<sha>
+    - uses: actions/download-artifact@<sha>
+      with:
+        path: evidence/
+    - run: node scripts/pr-summary.mjs evidence/ > pr-summary.md
+    - run: cat pr-summary.md >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
+    - uses: marocchino/sticky-pull-request-comment@<sha>
+      with:
+        header: pr-summary
+        path: pr-summary.md
+```
+
+`if: always()` is non-negotiable — the comment must produce signal
+even when upstream jobs fail. The summary script must fall back to
+"—" rather than abort when an artifact is missing.
+
+### Per-PR HTML reports on GitHub Pages
+
+Each PR gets a stable, mobile-Safari-browsable URL hosting the
+rendered report HTML:
+
+```
+https://<owner>.github.io/<repo>/pr/<N>/
+  ├── jacoco/             — JaCoCo backend coverage
+  ├── frontend-coverage/  — Karma + Istanbul
+  ├── playwright/         — Playwright HTML report
+  └── index.html          — landing page with three sub-links
+```
+
+Implementation: a `publish-pr-reports` job runs after `test` + `e2e`
+(PR-only), downloads the three HTML artifact dirs, stages them under
+`pr/<N>/{jacoco,frontend-coverage,playwright}/` plus a small
+`index.html`, and pushes to a `gh-pages` branch via
+`peaceiris/actions-gh-pages`. `keep_files: true` preserves other
+open PRs' subtrees on the same branch.
+
+```yaml
+publish-pr-reports:
+  if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'
+  needs: [test, e2e]
+  permissions:
+    contents: write
+  steps:
+    - uses: actions/checkout@<sha>
+    - uses: actions/download-artifact@<sha>
+      with:
+        path: incoming/
+        pattern: '{jacoco-report,frontend-coverage,playwright-html-report}'
+    - name: Stage under pr/<N>/
+      run: |
+        dest="pr-reports/pr/${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}"
+        mkdir -p "$dest"
+        cp -r incoming/jacoco-report "$dest/jacoco" || true
+        cp -r incoming/frontend-coverage "$dest/frontend-coverage" || true
+        cp -r incoming/playwright-html-report "$dest/playwright" || true
+        # write a tiny index.html linking the three subdirs
+    - uses: peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@<sha>
+      with:
+        github_token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
+        publish_dir: pr-reports/
+        publish_branch: gh-pages
+        keep_files: true
+```
+
+Combine with the sticky comment from the previous section: the
+`pr-summary` job picks up `needs.publish-pr-reports.result` and
+appends a "Reports:" line to the comment with three direct
+`https://<owner>.github.io/<repo>/pr/<N>/...` links. A reviewer on a
+phone taps from the PR comment into the rendered HTML — no log
+drill-down, no artifact download.
+
+One-time repo setup: **Settings → Pages → Source: Deploy from a
+branch → `gh-pages` → `/ (root)`**. The branch is created by the
+first PR run; Pages serving has to be toggled on manually.
+
+Stale `pr/<N>/` subtrees aren't auto-cleaned on PR close — wire a
+small `pull_request: closed` workflow that removes the directory if
+you care about long-term gh-pages hygiene.
+
+### Mobile-viewport e2e
+
+If the project ships a UI, run the existing Playwright suite under
+**both** desktop and mobile-device emulation. Catches mobile-layout
+regressions that aren't visible to a reviewer who only has a phone.
+
+```ts
+// playwright.config.ts
+import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';
+
+export default defineConfig({
+  use: {
+    screenshot: 'only-on-failure',
+    video: 'retain-on-failure',
+    trace: 'retain-on-failure',
+  },
+  projects: [
+    { name: 'chromium',     use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] } },
+    { name: 'mobile-safari', use: { ...devices['iPhone 14 Pro'] } },
+  ],
+});
+```
+
+iPhone device profiles default to **WebKit**, not Chromium, so the
+CI step has to install both browsers:
+
+```yaml
+- run: npx playwright install --with-deps chromium webkit
+- run: npm run test:e2e
+```
+
+Failure artifacts (screenshots, video, trace) are uploaded with the
+HTML report and surfaced via the per-PR Pages publish from the
+previous section. A failed mobile-safari test on a phone-only
+reviewer's PR now shows up as: red ✗ in the sticky comment → tap
+"Playwright" link → see the failing-spec screenshot inline.
+
